==English==

===Etymology===
Alteration of {{m|en|nuts}} to avoid vulgar {{m|en|nuts||testicles}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-nerts.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)ts}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|slang|euphemistic}} Crazy; [[nuts]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|title=Grosset and Dunlap present Show girl‎|page=47|author=Joseph Patrick McEvoy
|passage="You'd be plumb '''nerts'''" says he, "to think of it."}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|nerd}} {{qualifier|possible}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|slang|euphemistic}} [[nuts|Nuts]]! Expression of dismay.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=GIRL GOLFER TELLS OF BESTING PRINCE; Beatrice Gottlieb Returns With Trophies of Victory From British Heir|date=Aug 19, 1933|work=New York Times
|passage=FOUND HIM 'TERRIBLY NICE' She Wonders What He Thought When She Said, 'Oh, '''Nerts'''!' After a Bad Shot.}}

